      "id": "be-s12-calculus-optimization-c1",
      "heading": "From tables to functions",
      "explanation_md": "For continuous decisions, **instead of tables we use mathematical functions**.\n\nSuppose revenue and cost both depend on quantity:\n\n- TR = f(Q)\n- TC = f(Q)\n\nThen **profit** is:\n\n**π(Q) = TR(Q) - TC(Q)**\n\n**To arrive at the marginal quantities, differentiate this equation.**",
      "example_ids": [],
