    {
      "id": "be-s12-calculus-optimization-c5",
      "heading": "Three takeaways from the session",
      "explanation_md": "The professor closes with three rules that tie the whole session together:\n\n1. **Include all costs and benefits when making decisions** (that means **opportunity cost**, as in economic profit).\n2. **When decisions span time, compare apples to apples** (that means **PV analysis**: bring every amount to today's value).\n3. **Optimal economic decisions are made at the margin** (that means **marginal analysis**: MB versus MC, MR versus MC).",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [],
